  "worked_solution": "Let's sketch the given situation.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13934287/assets/2a3107d0db934d4dc9552444badc52914f92d46d7fd83a3e6048d06f3465dcf9.png)\n\nSince the line $y=5$ is a horizontal line, the shortest distance between this line and the point $(2,-3)$ is given by the absolute value of the difference between $y$-coordinate of the point and $5.$ \n\nSo, the shortest distance is\n\n$$\nd=|-3-5|=8.\n$$",
